{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=xsk-umem-rereads; Search only snapshots/s01. Within net/xdp and AF_XDP-capable driver TX-completion and metadata paths, find UMEM-resident fields (xsk descriptor addr/len/options, tx_metadata request fields, flags) that are fetched from the userspace-mapped shared memory more than once, or consumed without a single READ_ONCE-into-local snapshot, so the validated copy and the used copy can diverge under a racing userspace writer. Exclude the seed demonstration itself (xsk_skb_metadata csum_start/csum_offset caching). Save a structured artifact for s01 recording execution_status, candidate file/function evidence, or a concrete evidence-backed negative result."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=uapi-double-fetch; Search only snapshots/s01. Find syscall/ioctl/setsockopt/netlink (including compat) handler paths where the same user-memory location (a length, count, pointer, or union member) is fetched twice via get_user/copy_from_user/peek-style double fetches so validation and use can diverge under a concurrent userspace writer, violating the seed's single-fetch/validated-value-identity invariant. Save a structured artifact for s01 recording execution_status, candidate file/function evidence, or a concrete evidence-backed negative result."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=vm-shared-desc-rereads; Search only snapshots/s01. In virtio/vhost/vdpa/paravirt paths, find guest- or device-writable descriptor tables, virtio config space, or packet headers that are read multiple times (once checked, once used) or trusted across re-reads without snapshotting into a local, letting a racing guest or device substitute an unvalidated value into a security-sensitive use. Save a structured artifact for s01 recording execution_status, candidate file/function evidence, or a concrete evidence-backed negative result."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=csum-partial-consumer-trust; Search only snapshots/s01. Find consumers of skb->csum_start/skb->csum_offset/CHECKSUM_PARTIAL (software checksum helpers, tunnel/encapsulation copy paths, forwarding) that perform memory access or field arithmetic on those values without re-validating them against skb headroom/length, so any inconsistently validated producer becomes an out-of-bounds read or write. Save a structured artifact for s01 recording execution_status, candidate file/function evidence, or a concrete evidence-backed negative result."}
